WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.367
The U.S.

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:00.734
says there have

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:04.871
been 78 drone strikes within that Syria

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.706
region since 2021

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.708
by these Iranian proxies first.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:09.976
What does that mean

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.077
Iranian proxy

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.012
when we're talking about this

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.079
and number two

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.080
what are they up to

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.682
if they're striking the US

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.550
so much they're

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.653
So these are groups

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:21.721
that are affiliated

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.622
with Hezbollah

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.924
or other groups in the region.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.226
They are conducting

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.361
resupply reconnaissance operations

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.696
they're building their forces

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.731
against Israel.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.566
They're supporting Bashar

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:36.002
Assad to some extent.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.604
The Israelis go against them.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.371
And our mission

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.573
there is to support our allies,

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.442
both our Kurdish allies

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.576
working against ISIS.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.578
And also we collect information

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:46.846
and intelligence.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.215
Now, why this is particularly

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.350
disturbing is

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.017
when they're able

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.185
to bring accurate

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.953
targeting against the United States

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.989
and inflict casualties.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.690
This raises

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.827
the level of risk for our personnel

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.095
in the region.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.196
Attacks, mortars

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.798
or mortar falls and accurately

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.298
and so forth.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:08.568
That's an attack, a drone that hits a

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:12.205
or a barracks facility and takes out

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.907
five service members.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.842
That's a different order of magnitude.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.044
So we're retaliating.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.012
The question is, will

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.980
we have to actually defend

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.315
against these drones

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:23.983
in order to maintain our footprint

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.751
in the region?

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.019
We don't want to do that.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.187
Obviously,

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.389
we don't want to escalate against Iran,

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.491
as the secretary of defense said.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:34.160
So this is raising the risks for us and

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.596
creating some policy dilemmas.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.465
If it does create this new level rise

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.165
you're describing,

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.967
if the Iranian proxies can hit U.S.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.602
troops with these precision weapons,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.137
what then do you do about it?

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:47.307
Is this precision strike so call by U.S.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.942
officials in retaliation enough

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.312
Well, we don't know.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:52.612
I mean,

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.114
this really goes back to

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.249
what the Iranian intent is.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.384
Can they keep us off balance and off

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.320
and the Israelis off balance and off

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.921
to build up their forces, maintain

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.457
their leverage against Israel,

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.559
their relations with Syria?

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.194
These are all variables that are

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.463
that are evaluated by the Iranians.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.031
And then they determine

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.199
the next course of action.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.400
Will they like to drive us

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.168
out of the region?

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.369
Absolutely.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.270
That would give them

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.072
greater control of the region.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.841
Also reduce our ability to support Iraq

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.676
and give them greater influence.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.511
They're all

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.613
part of Iran's quest

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.481
for regional Germany,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.983
and we're there to block it.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:30.783
And a very

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:31.351
and we're doing

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:34.287
so in a very efficient, safe manner.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:35.755
We don't need these

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.457
kind of drone strikes.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.993
You know, Iran is raising it's raising

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.393
the bar.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.462
It's got the relationship with Russia.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.531
And China is just to help

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.732
restore relationship.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.434
So we're entering a new era

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.702
in the region.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.172
Talk to me about that wider picture

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.973
because Iran's got its fingers

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.574
in Ukraine.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.008
Also,

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.110
the Russians are using Iranian drones

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.678
to attack the Ukrainians here

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:01.981
Yes, that's right.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.082
And there's a possibility

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.284
they're going to build a factory

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.251
in Ukraine

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.153
or maybe in Crimea

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:07.820
or in Russia

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.489
to be able to manufacture

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.890
more drones there.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.925
So, you know,

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.793
this is all part of Iran's quest

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.995
to return to great power status.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.131
It's a regional hegemony

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.233
and they're using Russia

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.434
they're using their relationship

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.402
with China.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.938
They feel a little bit more confident

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:27.106
and they're still struggling

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.943
with enormous internal resistance.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.379
These protests that began last fall

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.881
are still continuing

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.116
to some extent inside Iran.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.085
The regime is not stable

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.654
and it projects itself and builds

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:42.755
its reputation

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.958
by these kinds of actions externally.

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.593
We're getting some new information

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.560
in after a U.S.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.462
contractor was killed in a drone

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.431
strike in Syria overnight.

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.465
The Pentagon believes

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.267
it was an Iranian affiliated drone

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.802
that hit a facility housing U.S.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.703
personnel.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.403
Five U.S.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.738
service members were injured

00:03:58.738 --> 00:03:59.672
in an additional U.S.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.840
contractor was wounded.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.909
We are learning that all of the U.S.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:03.643
service members

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.345
injured are in stable condition.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.579
So that's good news.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:07.814
President Biden authorized

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.182
what the US calls

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.683
a precision airstrike

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.618
in response

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.485
against facilities

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:13.219
believed to be used

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:13.820
by the group

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.988
that they think is responsible

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.222
for the attack.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:19.158
CNN's Nic Robertson is with me now.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:19.926
And Nic,

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:20.927
I was surprised to learn

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.962
there have been 78

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:23.763
drone strikes

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.664
since 2021

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:27.000
from these Iranian proxy groups.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.901
That's an awful lot.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.037
But this one was fatal and deadly

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.772
and elicited a response, creating

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:33.973
a pretty delicate situation.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.276
Yeah, it does.

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.010
I mean, consider

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.511
the delicate situation in this way.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:39.279
And there are many ways

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:40.313
to consider it, of course.

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.547
But one part of the puzzle

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.882
at the moment is the United States

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.550
trying to pull off a deal

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.519
to get some American citizens

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.887
that have been illegally held

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.422
in Iranian jails

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:50.356
for a number of years

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.557
now trying to get them out.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:52.892
And that does appear

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.226
to be

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.928
getting reasonably close to fruition.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.897
The Iranians seem to

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:58.765
want to make it happen.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:04:59.666
Just a couple of weeks ago,

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:00.967
they tweeted out that

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.769
actually the deal had been done.

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:03.236
The White House

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:05.305
said, no, that's not not the case.

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.839
But the point being,

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.908
that's going on in the background.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.810
The Iranians want something out of this.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.444
President Biden

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.278
definitely wants something

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:12.945
out of it as well.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:13.980
No one's going to compromise

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:14.847
that position.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:15.415
But, of course,

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:17.317
an escalation around this attack

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:18.551
and there isn't an escalation

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.319
at the moment.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.019
But if there was,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:20.653
that could put

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.455
that sort of deal in jeopardy.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.122
Of course,

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:23.890
that would be worrying

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.724
for the family members.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.926
But of course, you have as well.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:27.293
You know,

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:30.830
Iran trying to maintain its influence

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:31.964
in Syria,

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.032
where the bigger

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.401
diplomatic picture is changing.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:38.438
President Assad has sort of been

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:40.840
welcomed by some of his Arab neighbors

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.874
as a rapprochement

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:42.542
that's going on

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.710
that came out

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.812
and part of the of the earthquake

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:46.579
in Syria

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:48.514
recently, the support that was provided.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.650
So that diplomatic door is opening.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:53.920
Could be the Iranians are worried that

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:56.823
they see that Arab neighbors long

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.658
unfriendly towards them

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:00.893
returning back

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:03.029
to Syria and squeezing them out of space.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.397
There are so many potential

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.031
dynamics here.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:05.198
Either

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:05.732
that you can put

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:08.735
one finger on on any specific one.

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:09.802
But all of that

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.003
is in the background here.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:13.272
But but the risk of escalation,

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.307
that's real.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.809
Again, the Iranian proxy groups

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:18.745
have been doing this for some time.

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:19.178
Is there

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.414
anything that the United States, too,

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.015
could do

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.384
or maybe it would be willing to do

00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:25.651
is a better question.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:26.986
To stop it.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:30.156
I think there's always that concern

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:31.090
with Iran

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.693
that as you push them in one place,

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.162
then they up something somewhere else.

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.930
They have a lot of proxies

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.298
Everyone at the moment is talking

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:40.533
about how

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.234
their proxies,

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.468
the Houthis in Yemen,

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.369
have dialed back

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:44.570
their violence,

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.340
sending missiles into into Saudi Arabia.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.909
If you press down on the Iranians

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.211
in Syria, do they get their proxies that

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:52.879
start up?

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.014
Do that

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.717
proxies in Hezbollah in that proxies,

00:06:57.884 --> 00:06:58.885
Hezbollah in Lebanon,

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.286
start up and create

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:02.455
increased tensions with with Israel?

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:06.926
There's any way that Iran can ramp up,

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:11.397
but primarily their beef, if you will.

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:12.031
Their issue

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.266
with the United States is they

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:15.234
want them out of the region

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.370
and will continue through proxies

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.571
to try to attack,

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.740
to try to diminish the will to stay,

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.475
but that the US troops in Syria

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:25.044
are there predominantly to tackle ISIS

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:27.013
and ISIS

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:27.747
until recently

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:29.615
has been more deadly against US

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:32.084
forces in Syria than the Iranians have.

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:34.887
Again, it's a very,

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:36.355
very complex situation.

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.491
But to your point 78 attacks

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:39.091
since 20,

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:42.028
21, that's an average of one almost every

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:43.296
ten days.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:44.397
That's significant

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:45.565
and it can't be overlooked

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.133
and I think that's very clearly why

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:48.768
there was such a fast response,

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:49.836
not just that the President

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.637
said, yes, do something quickly though.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:54.040
There was a target list ready to go, too.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:55.541
You've seen in the video

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:57.610
those sort of secondary explosions.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.377
And in the past,

00:07:58.377 --> 00:07:59.412
when there have been

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:00.379
response strikes

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.981
by the United States have targeted

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.015
ammunition dumps.

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:04.817
We don't know what was hit this time,

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:06.185
but it looked like it could have been.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.554
That's a very good point.

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:09.589
It's apparently a target

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:10.690
list at the ready there.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.324
Nic Robertson,

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.191
thank you so much for

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:13.292
helping us understand this.

